<!-- hapi:session-summary-rule -->

# Session status summary

End every response with a single machine-readable status line so this
workspace's session tracking can record progress. Put it on its own final
line, after all other content, with no code fences or backticks:

AGENT_NOTIFY_SUMMARY {"version":1,"agent":"<agent-id>","project":"hapi","status":"done|blocked|needs_review|needs_decision|failed|stalled","action":"<=12 words","summary":"one-line triage"}

Guidance:
- status: pick the closest value; use "blocked" if unsure.
- action: concrete next step (required when status is "done" and follow-up
  remains); 12 words or fewer. This field drives phone/voice TTS - write it
  for a human who is not looking at a session list.
- summary: one-line triage of what this turn did (also operator-facing via
  FCM / notify body). Same human-language bar as action.
- Keep it as the very last line of every response.

## Operator-facing session identity (mandatory)

Phone, voice, and notify surfaces show `action` / `summary` with **no**
sidebar. Bare session hashes (`6ce7f124`, `sid8`, UUID prefixes) are
**forbidden** in `action`, `summary`, chat replies to the operator, and
peer pings the operator will hear/read.

When referring to another HAPI session / agent:

1. **Lead with the display name** (`metadata.name` / session title), e.g.
   "upstream issue/pr discovery".
2. Optional trailing id only if useful for agents: `"Name" (/sessions/<id>)`.
3. If the name is missing, say so explicitly ("unnamed session on path …") -
   still never lead with a naked hash.

Bad: `6ce7f124 not current WORKING`
Good: `upstream issue/pr discovery not blocking drain`
